America/Inuvik moved to permanent UTC-6 on 21 August 2026. IANA 2026d models
this as standard time after its temporary CLDR workaround ends in November.
Represent it instead as UTC-7 plus one hour of permanent DST, keeping the
America_Mountain metazone and Mountain Daylight Time display name.

Retain the distant abbreviation transition used for America/Edmonton: MDT
changes to MouT on 8 March 2100 without changing the UTC offset or DST state.
This preserves compatibility with Android implementations that lack the
ZoneInfoData permanent DST fix, even though this checkout already has that fix.

See 002-northamerica.info and 003-northamerica.info.
